65.m:
A wise man should carefully perform [a vow] on the eleventh according to the rule,
for a year, beginning from the bright fortnight of Mārgaśīrṣa;
that vow is dear to the giver of wealth, and when performed, bestows riches. / 65.6

Thus, beginning in the bright fortnight of Phālguna, the wise man [performs it];
on the fourteenth, particularly in the dark fortnight, is the vow dedicated to Rudra,
beginning from the month of Māgha for a full year, O king. / 65.9

Even a single vow, when performed, constantly destroys sins;
he, on the other hand, who performs all this, O son of the best of men,
he, pure and free from passion, reaches all the worlds, O king. / 65.13

66.m:
Agastya said:
The Lord, Janārdana himself, is the true wonder;
indeed, many and diverse wonders of his have been seen. / 66.2

Nārada said:
"For one thousand years I have meditated on you, O Lord of the universe;
if you are pleased with me, O Acyuta, tell me that by which you may be attained." / 66.9
